.TH CCLIST 1 "2026-07-17" "codecommit-utils" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cclist \- list AWS CodeCommit repositories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cclist
.RB [ \-\-create\-repos\-md ]
.RB [ \-\-help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cclist
lists the AWS CodeCommit repositories in the current account and region, one
name per line.
.PP
It is a thin wrapper around
.BR cch (1),
which holds the implementation:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cclist                    is  cch repo list
cclist \-\-create\-repos\-md   is  cch repo list \-\-md
.fi
.RE
.PP
Both spellings are fully supported.
.BR cch (1)
is the recommended entry point for new work, and documents the behaviour in
detail.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-create\-repos\-md
Write a
.B REPOS.md
file in the current directory listing each repository with its description,
instead of printing names. Repositories without a description are recorded as
"No description available". If the account has no repositories, no file is
written.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Display help and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AWS_PROFILE
The AWS profile whose credentials and region are used, as for the AWS CLI.
.TP
.B AWS_REGION
The AWS region to operate in, as for the AWS CLI.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Exits 0 on success, and 1 on an unknown option or when the underlying AWS CLI
call fails.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cch (1),
.BR ccclone (1),
.BR ccinit (1),
.BR aws (1)
